    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0389" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.415C/74a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">South</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-06-24T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1926—2
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>52. Associated Press despatch from Panama dated June 22, states that a resolution
                    recommending common action by Pan American states against any aggressor state
                    has been unanimously adopted by the Bolívar Congress.</p>
                <p>Please report fully. In this connection refer to Department’s telegram 33, April
                    24, 2 p.m. 1925, your 50, April 28, 3 p.m. 1925, Department’s 320, June 17,
                    1925, your 854, October 31, 1925,<anchor n="56" xml:id="d133-f1"/> and further
                    correspondence regarding assurance of Panaman Government that the Congress is
                    purely ceremonial.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d133-f1" n="56" xml:id="d133-f1-content">
                <p>Last two telegrams not printed.</p>
            </note>
